## Trains: Passenger Assist

**Passenger Assist** is a free service on the rail network. Staff can help you get on and off trains, with luggage, and to change trains. You can:

- **book ahead**, up to **2 hours** before your journey, using the Passenger Assist app, website or by phone
- or **turn up and go**, and ask staff at the station

## Flying: special assistance

UK law gives you the right to **free assistance at airports** and on flights if you have a disability or reduced mobility, including hidden disabilities. Tell your airline at least **48 hours** before you fly. Help can include getting through the airport, security and boarding.

## The Hidden Disabilities Sunflower

A **Sunflower lanyard** is a discreet way to show you may need extra help, time or patience. It is recognised at many airports, stations, supermarkets and venues. Many places give them out for free.

## Coaches and taxis

- National Express offers a **Disabled Coachcard** with money off coach fares.
- Licensed taxis and private hire vehicles **must not refuse** assistance dog owners, and in England and Wales, drivers of designated wheelchair accessible vehicles must help wheelchair users and not charge extra.
- Some councils run **taxi voucher** or **dial-a-ride** schemes for people who cannot use buses.
